# Test run artifacts — machine-generated test output (checkpoint.jsonl,
# failures.txt, summary.json, build.log) from pi5_test_suite.sh. These are
# per-run artifacts that bloat the repo and go stale; they should not be
# committed. If you need to share test results, paste them in a PR comment
# or attach to a release.
#
# EXCEPTION (Task 9-c): test_results/history/ IS committed. It holds an
# append-only archive of prior summary.json snapshots (one per rebuild)
# used by scripts/show_trend.py to plot pass-rate trends across rebuilds.
# Each file is <1 KB; the directory grows by ~1 KB per suite run, which is
# acceptable for trend visibility. The per-run summary.json itself is still
# ignored (overwritten in place each run).
test_results/*
!test_results/history/
!test_results/history/**

/tmp/vuma_results/
/tmp/qemu_bins/
/tmp/qemu/

